<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had sown 52.5 percent of their 1997/98 wheat crop by July 11, the Agriculture Secretariat said in its weekly report Thursday.</p>
<p>This compared with  72.6 percent completion of a larger sown area by the same date last season. Sowing is stil being delayed by drought in Cordoba province and southern and central Santa Fe, as well as by excessive rain in the key province of Buenos Aires. Farmers had sown 54.4 percent of their intended area of 113,100 hectares of linseed by July 11, and 90,000 hectares out of an intended 258,000 hectares of brewers barley.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..............</p>
<p> Wheat     6,250  52.5  (72.6)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)</p>
<p> Maize     3,952  100.0(100.0) 3,160.5   97.3  (96.0)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,648  100.0(100.0) 6,346.9  100.0 (100.0)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,048  100.0(100.0) 2,936.2  100.0 (100.0)</p>
<p> Sorghum     805  100.0(100.0)   677.2   99.2  (99.4)</p>
<p> Cotton	956  100.0  (n/a)   834.2   94.1  (88.8)</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
